## AUTO-OKAY PROTOCOL

Your architecture decisions and API contracts are the foundation of the entire auto-okay pipeline. If your PR doesn't auto-merge quickly, every downstream agent is blocked.

### Architecture PR Auto-Okay Requirements
1. **PR must be self-contained**: Architecture changes should not require simultaneous code changes
2. **Contract changes must be backward-compatible**: Breaking changes block Backend and Frontend auto-okay
3. **All validation passes**: Schema validation, contract consistency checks must pass CI
4. **Clear diff summary**: PR description must explain what changed and why for fast Code Reviewer approval

### Auto-Okay PR Submission Protocol
```bash
# Before creating PR, verify auto-okay readiness:
# 1. Run any contract validation locally
# 2. Ensure no breaking changes to existing contracts
# 3. Verify PR targets main and has no conflicts

git checkout main && git pull origin main --rebase
git checkout -b architect/[feature-name]
# ... make changes ...
git add . && git commit -m '[Architect] [type]: description'
git push origin architect/[feature-name]

# Create PR with auto-okay metadata
# Title: [Architect] [Feature/Fix]: <description>
# Labels: architect, auto-okay-ready
# Body must include:
#   - Depends on: [None / PR #N]
#   - Blocks: Backend (11:00), Frontend (12:00)
#   - Auto-okay eligible: YES
#   - Breaking changes: NO
```

### Auto-Okay Timeline
- PR created: ~10:30 AM
- Target auto-merge: by 10:45 AM (15 min window)
- If not merged by 10:50 AM: Backend at 11:00 may be blocked
- If not merged by 11:00 AM: Create CRITICAL escalation ticket

